File Index

/emit.ts
Purpose: AreaFile → canonical .are text emitter (letter-form flag vectors, doors 0-9 since Phase 12b, doors-before-extra-descriptions room sub-block order, M/R script entries, LF line endings); EmitError on inexpressible models.

/groups-stock.ts
Purpose: Generated stock groups.dat table (STOCK_GROUPS) — checked in, mirrors const.c group_table. Regenerate with `pnpm --filter @shatteredarchive/merc-area gen-skills-stock` (scripts/gen-skills-stock.ts, Phase 15) — the file's OWN interface StockGroupRow is the canonical definition (groups.ts imports it FROM here, the reverse of skills-stock.ts's direction).

/groups.test.ts
Purpose: groups.dat parse/emit/validate tests: stock round trip, prefix member resolution, cycle guard, rating sentinels.

/groups.ts
Purpose: groups.dat overlay format — parse/emit/validate (prefix member resolution against skills+groups, cycle = error, -1/0/1+ rating sentinels) + stockGroupsFile.

/index.ts
Purpose: Public package surface — re-exports types, parse/emit, Reader, validation (scripts/refs incl. Phase 11 resolver hook + collectDefinedEntities), skills and groups modules, (Phase 13) simulateResets + its result/option types, (Phase 14a) spell-spec/spell-codegen, and (Phase 14c) parseLiveSnapshot/diffSpawnState.

/live-state.test.ts
Purpose: live-state.ts tests: parseLiveSnapshot's tolerant-parse contract (well-formed, non-JSON, torn/truncated, wrong-shape all -> null), diffSpawnState cases (clean world = zero drift, killed mob w/ no live room entry at all, the SimMobGroup per-vnum-sum trap, player-dropped object, door opened, a sim-only door with no live data yet is skipped not a false mismatch).

/live-state.ts
Purpose: Live world-state snapshot parsing + boot-vs-live drift diff (Phase 14c) — parseLiveSnapshot(text) tolerantly parses state_snapshot.c's vnum/count-only JSON (malformed -> null, never throws); diffSpawnState(sim, live) compares merc-area's own simulateResets() output against a live snapshot over the UNION of rooms either side mentions, summing SimMobGroup.count per vnum before comparing (groups are loadout-grouped), yielding missingMobs/extraObjects/missingObjects/players/doorChanges per drifted room plus a summary. Doors only compare where the sim actually defines one — a live room the builder hasn't hot-reloaded yet is silently skipped, never a false mismatch.

/parse.test.ts
Purpose: Parser unit tests per section kind plus error-position assertions.

/parse.ts
Purpose: .are text → AreaFile parser mirroring db.c consumption (section registry, tilde strings, dice/flag vectors; doors 0-9 and R room-script entries since Phase 12b); ParseError carries line context.

/reader.ts
Purpose: Token/line reader over raw area text (tilde-terminated strings, numbers with letter-form flag vectors via flagConvert) — the parsing substrate.

/refs.test.ts
Purpose: validateRefs/collectDefinedEntities tests: fully-linked clean file, in-range dangling = error (even when a resolver could resolve it), out-of-range = warning without a resolver, resolver turns proven refs into external links and unresolved ones into "any listed area" warnings, soft exit-key semantics, stock-corpus sweep (no save-blocking errors).

/roundtrip.test.ts
Purpose: The load-bearing guarantee: every area.lst file parses → emits → re-parses byte-identically (canonical form).

/scripts.test.ts
Purpose: Script validation tests: trigger vocabulary, mob-in-file attachment, body budget, preserved-verbatim unknown resets.

/simulate.test.ts
Purpose: simulateResets tests, each keyed to a specific db.c reset_area branch: M+E+G chain, global vs room-local M limits, O dedup, P container chaining (incl. onto a just-given, not-yet-in-a-room object), D lock states 0/1/2 defaulting doors to open, R marker (no reordering), the mob==null vs !last orphan-G/E distinction (only the former warns, matching db.c's own bug() call), cross-area resolver, identical-loadout grouping.

/simulate.ts
Purpose: Reset simulator (Phase 13) — simulateResets(area, {resolveExternal}) computes FIRST-BOOT-ONLY spawn state (per-room mobs w/ equipped+carried, room objects w/ nested P contents, door states, randomized-exit markers, warnings) as a line-faithful mirror of db.c reset_area's M/O/P/G/E/D/R state machine incl. the shared last/LastMob threaded across the whole reset list. Deliberately not modeled (documented in the file header): the P/G/E object-limit's 1-in-5 random bypass (always deterministic-skip instead), shop-keeper unlimited restock, pet-shop/cost/alignment-zap side effects, container lock write-back.

/skills-stock.ts
Purpose: Generated stock skills tables (STOCK_SKILLS, SKILL_SPELL_FUNS, STOCK_FUN_TARGET_PAIRS) — mirrors const.c skill_table; regenerate after ANY live redeploy that adds a skill_table row (e.g. an applied codegen spell patch — Phase 14a's own "spark bolt" sat un-synced here for a day, invisible to the Skills page, until 2026-07-25). The original gen-skills-stock.js was never checked in (a Phase 7 scratchpad one-off) and this gap recurred; Phase 15 (2026-07-25) promoted a from-scratch parser into a permanent, checked-in `scripts/gen-skills-stock.ts` (`pnpm --filter @shatteredarchive/merc-area gen-skills-stock`) covering both this file and groups-stock.ts — watch for adjacent C string-literal concatenation (two "..." tokens back to back, no comma) and literal raw control bytes (not \t escapes) inside message strings, both of which a naive single-quoted-string regex will mis-parse; the permanent script handles both.

/skills.test.ts
Purpose: skills.dat parse/emit/validate tests: stock round trip, (fun,target) stock-pair guard, malformed rows.

/skills.ts
Purpose: skills.dat overlay format — parse/emit/validate ((fun,target) must be a stock-proven pair — boot crash guard) + stockSkillsFile/stockSkill.

/spell-codegen.test.ts
Purpose: spell-codegen.ts golden-file tests (Phase 14a): byte-exact per-archetype .c function + const.c row fixtures, alphabetical anchor logic (incl. the before/after distinction for const.c's multi-line entries), overlay-row round trip through skills.ts's real emitter/parser.

/spell-codegen.ts
Purpose: SpellSpec → reviewable 4-section C patch (Phase 14a) — magic.h decl + magic.c function + skills_data.c fun_registry line + a NEW const.c skill_table row (skills.dat can only overlay data on an EXISTING row, never introduce one — see file header). Anchors are quoted verbatim source lines, never line numbers; const.c anchors "before" the alphabetical successor's opening line (its entries are multi-line, so "after" a predecessor's opening line would land mid-entry). generateOverlayRow's SkillEntry output is the "what this looks like once deployed" preview, fed into the const.c row — never written live to skills.dat.

/spell-spec.test.ts
Purpose: SpellSpec model tests (Phase 14a): archetype/target compatibility matrix, naming collisions, field bounds, C-string/skills.dat-line safety.

/spell-spec.ts
Purpose: Declarative NEW-spell spec model (Phase 14a) — closed archetype set (damage/buff/debuff/heal/cure) each lifted from a real stock spell body (spell_flamestrike/spell_acid_blast, spell_armor, spell_blindness, spell_cure_light, spell_cure_blindness), validateSpellSpec (naming/target/field-bounds checks). Builder metadata only — the game never reads a stored spec; see spell-codegen.ts for what actually gets deployed.

/types.ts
Purpose: The AreaFile model: every section kind (area header, mobiles, objects, rooms w/ exits+extra descrs, resets, shops, specials, helps, socials, scripts) as typed records mirroring db.c field order; Phase 12b: RoomExit.door 0-9, MobScript.attach 'mob'|'room' (R entries) + ROOM_SCRIPT_TRIGGERS.

/validate.ts
Purpose: Semantic validation beyond syntax — validateScripts (trigger vocabulary incl. the room branch + #SCRIPTS-after-#ROOMS order guard, budgets), collectRefs/validateRefs (in-range dangling = error, out-of-range = warning, or with the Phase 11 opts.resolveExternal hook: proven refs → structured RefsSummary.external links, unresolved → "any listed area" warnings; Phase 12b adds D/R reset bound errors mirroring db.c exit(1) and `warp <vnum>` body targets as room refs), collectDefinedEntities (world-index surface), vnumsOutsideRange (header shrink guard), isKnownSpecFun, shop/special duplicate semantics.
